orch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested on Windows 11, this PR mostly works as expected, but I have some suggestions:\r\n- I think this PR should also handle the newly added `Input.set_joy_light()` that changes the LED light on a controller:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/78c6632eb174aabb2790975cf83e28fee065b43d/core/input/input.cpp#L1007-L1014 (EDIT: And controller motion sensors)\r\n- If you use `Input.is_action_pressed()` to check for action presses, hold the button on your controller that activates the action and then disable the joypad input while still holding the button, the action will stay pressed.\r\nThere's an Input method called `Input::release_pressed_events()`, but it will also release the non-joypad events too, so I'm not too sure if we can use it.\r\nI made a PR that saves the action event types ( https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115099 ), maybe it's possible to use that functionality to check if an action is being pressed only because of a joypad press/axis movement, and if it is, release the action.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105513#pullrequestreview-3682639362","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105513","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105513#pullrequestreview-36826393